<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andijan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andijan is a city in the eastern Fergana valley of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, one of the oldest towns of the region and the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>. It was a seat of the Timurid rulers of Fergana and later part of the Khanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a>. In May 2005 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> security forces fired on protesters in its main square, killing hundreds of people, an event known as the Andijan massacre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andijan.jpg" alt="Andijan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Petar Milošević · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devonaboy_Jome_Mosque,_Andijan,_Uzbekistan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
